<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Vietnam</h1><p class="st-meta">1949 CE – 1955 CE · capital Saigon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The French-sponsored Vietnamese state of former emperor Bao Dai, created in 1949 as a non-communist rival to Ho Chi Minh's government.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elysee-accords">Elysee Accords</a> of March 1949, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> recognised a State of Vietnam within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-fourth-republic">French Union</a>, uniting <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-tonkin">Tonkin</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-annam">Annam</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-cochinchina">Cochinchina</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> as head of state. It replaced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/provisional-central-government-of-vietnam">Provisional Central Government of Vietnam</a> and was recognised by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in 1950.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state, based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a>, gained ministries, its own army and currency, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> kept control of defence and foreign policy until 1954. Its authority was challenged by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> in the countryside and by armed religious sects, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caodaism">Cao Dai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoa-hao">Hoa Hao</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binh-xuyen">Binh Xuyen</a> gang in Saigon. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> spent much of his time in France and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/da-lat">Da Lat</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-geneva">Geneva</a> Accords of 1954 limited the state to the south of the 17th parallel. Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-dinh-diem">Ngo Dinh Diem</a> defeated the sects and in October 1955 won a rigged referendum deposing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a>, proclaiming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-vietnam">Republic of Vietnam</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-vietnam.jpg" alt="State of Vietnam" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: (many, see history) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Vietnam.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1949 CE – 1955 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Saigon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bao Dai, Ngo Dinh Diem</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Quốc gia Việt Nam</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=state-of-vietnam" aria-label="State of Vietnam on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7619 1775 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Vietnam lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7939 2031L7939 2031M7939 2031L7939 2031M7939 2031L5054 728M7939 2031L7939 2031"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7939 2031h0M7939 2031h0M5054 728h0M7939 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7939 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7939 2031h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Saigon. <a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=state-of-vietnam">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
